11	 * deterministically from {@code (lastName, postcode)} (see {@link AssignHousehold}), two
12	 * owners that share a last name and postcode are the same household. A second owner in an
13	 * existing household is therefore rejected as a household duplicate (409) — <em>unless</em>
14	 * the request opts in via {@code sharesHousehold}, which declares the new owner a member of
15	 * that household and bypasses the block.
16	 *
17	 * <p>Runs after {@link BuildOwner} and {@link AssignHousehold} (so the new owner carries its
18	 * computed {@code householdId}) and before {@link SaveOwner} (so a duplicate is a 409 rather
19	 * than a persisted record).
20	 */
21	public class CheckOwnerIdentityUnique {
